From 00011abbf2fb310b91f44ab355923c1f2b3cdad0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:49:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0230 diagnostic: allocator grow probe logging
 container/size/count/aligned/aux/site at the costume abort path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Explorer/Football/Mechanic abort is a deliberate SDK abort in the
grow branch of allocator 0x954310 (REPORT-LOG108-LOG109.md §7): a
container's inline buffer cannot hold the request (or a count/size
overflows), so it calls the heap's grow virtual function V, which aborts.
V's identity and assertion condition are not pinned by static
disassembly, and the discriminating test (log-115) proved the trigger is
on the BODY/clothes side, not the cap.

Two FRAME_STEP cuts in 0x954310, one per grow entry that reaches the
virtual call: 0x954478 (the shared tail: ldr x8, [x0], reached from the
bump-overflow entry 0x954428 and the space-check entry 0x954468) and
0x954390 (the overflow entry 0x954370's own ldr x8, [x0]; that entry
calls V inline and never reaches the shared tail). Each cut's trampoline
passes the grow parameters to one shared body, which appends a 64-byte
record (container, size, count, aligned size, aux, site, seq written
last) to a ring in the frame-step state page at +0x3B20 (immediately
after the 0228 headkey ring, which ends at +0x3B20; the state page is
0x4000 bytes). The aux field is [sp,#0x28] at the cut, which the three
grow entries fill differently (overflow: count; bump-overflow:
[container,#0x90]*count; space-check: -([container,#0x90]*count)), so
aux + count identifies which grow condition fired. The body writes the
'GRWR' magic at ring+0 first (the 0228 DHKY bug: the stub never wrote
its magic, so eight device runs logged zero lines). The host drains the
ring once per present (dm_diag_grow_frame_tick, tag 'diag-grow') and
logs every record. Logging-only: the body writes nothing but the ring,
touches no callee-saved register and no flag, and executes the replaced
instruction before branching back. Temporary: remove the cuts and the
drain once the abort trigger is pinned.
---
 dm/games/0100000000010000/patches.py | 151 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 dm/host/hud_manual.c                 |  70 +++++++++++++
 dm/host/hud_manual.h                 |   5 +
 dm/host/uw.c                         |   1 +
 dm/tools/nso_asm.py                  |   1 +
 5 files changed, 227 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

